From 07b42a5aa3969f49003b2db3ab8a9dcedd4825eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:30:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] ech_dns: ECH configs from HTTPS records over DoH;
 pem_files

With `ech_dns` set to a DNS-over-HTTPS endpoint (RFC 8484, e.g.
https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query), the transport gives epoxy-tls an
ech_resolver that asks it for each name's HTTPS record (RFC 9460) through
the client itself and hands over the record's ech config list, so a
connection to a site that publishes one offers real Encrypted Client Hello
as Chrome does. One query per name at a time, kept for the record's TTL (60
s to a day; 5 minutes without a record); a connection waits at most 1.5 s
for the answer and then goes out with GREASE. The DoH server's own name,
addresses and names that are never public are not asked. Unset, nothing
changes.

`pem_files` (epoxy's own option for extra trusted certificates) is passed
through too, so a test can trust its own CA.
